      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day. That is twice the maximum labeled daily dose for adults of 3,200 mg/day. The 1,600 mg single dose is also well above the usual maximum of 800 mg per dose. At this level the risks of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up substantially, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nThese are standard prescription-strength options within the labeled limits:\n- **800 mg by mouth 4 times daily**, for a total of 3,200 mg/day. This is the maximum, and it is usually reserved for short-term use in inflammatory conditions.\n- **600 mg by mouth 4 times daily**, for a total of 2,400 mg/day.\n- **400 mg by mouth 4 times daily**, for a total of 1,600 mg/day. This is common for pain or fever.\n\nYou may have meant 1600 mg total per day, for example 400 mg four times daily. If so, tell me and I'll enter it. Tell me which regimen you want, or whether you want a different agent, and I'll enter it right away."
      }
